        "main_text_has_explicit_synthesis": true,
        "si_used": false,
        "procedure": "One-pot aerobic reaction of basic chromium(III) acetate [Cr3(OH)2(OAc)7] and Dy(OAc)3·4H2O in a 1:1 metal ratio with 2.0 eq. of Hbda in MeCN under reflux, followed by addition of 2.2 eq. of 3-(methylthio)propionic acid (Hprop·SMe). Oxalate and glycolate ligands form in situ by aerobic catalytic oxidation of acetate; direct addition of oxalic and glycolic acids did not afford crystalline product. Detailed quantities and work-up are referred to the ESI. Octahedrally shaped crystals of 1 are obtained.",
